  "agy_derivation": "meter_quota_share.py over /root/agy-quota/calls.csv, 2026-10-13T07:01 to 2026-10-24T05:30 (10.94 days): 83,551 calls succeeded and 1,936 hit the cap (so the stretch used the whole allowance) = 229,190 calls per 30 days. Cross-check: median 1,578 calls in the 5 h before a 429 burst = 227,232 per 30 days. Every agy model is counted as one call of one pool, as the meter counts them. A second reading, the median calls in the 24 h before a lock (status.json past_bursts prev24h: 5,771), gives 173K per 30 days: the share is between 4.4e-6 and 5.8e-6 a call.",
  "unused_quota_value": 1.0,
  "unused_quota_note": "1.0 = a call is worth its full share. Quota left unused at a reset is worth nothing, so near a reset with quota to spare this falls toward 0 (set it per run).",
  "claude_pricing": "Per PAGE and per model (Derek, 2026-10-26, #6740): the old 0.0303 points a call, from 66 Sonnet TEXT calls, priced Opus as Sonnet and an image call as a text call. Each Claude route now carries claude_points_per_page; null = UNMETERED, never routed on cost. Opus and Sonnet image OCR are unmetered until job route-judge-run-6740 posts points per image call on #6740. Measured Opus rates, for the stages that use them (estimator v2, scripts/eval/estimator/chain/capacity.json): correction (correct.mjs, 10 pages a call) 1% of an account-week per 250 Latin pages = 0.004 points a page (#5924, 2026-10-24); translation (10 pages a call) 3% per 3,250 pages = 0.00092 points a page (#7263)."
